Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that

$$
\begin{aligned}T(v+kw)=T(v)+T(kw)=T(v)+kT(w)\end{aligned}
$$

for any vectors $v$ and $w.$ Therefore,

$$
\begin{aligned}T({v}_{1}+3{v}_{2}) & =T({v}_{1})+3T({v}_{2}) \\ [\begin{aligned}15 \\ 6\end{aligned}] & =[\begin{aligned}6 \\ -12\end{aligned}]+3T({v}_{2}) \\ 3T({v}_{2}) & =[\begin{aligned}15 \\ 6\end{aligned}]-[\begin{aligned}6 \\ -12\end{aligned}] \\ 3T({v}_{2}) & =[\begin{aligned}9 \\ 18\end{aligned}] \\ T({v}_{2}) & =\frac{1}{3}[\begin{aligned}9 \\ 18\end{aligned}] \\ T({v}_{2}) & =[\begin{aligned}3 \\ 6\end{aligned}].\end{aligned}
$$

